    [Doc] Remove explicit engine IDs from documentation (#19005)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    As reported in #18701, vLLM can pass `engine_id` twice when constructing
    a child KV transfer configuration that explicitly sets it, causing a
    `TypeError`.
    
    The deployment examples do not require manually assigned engine IDs.
    This PR removes explicit `engine_id` values and the related assignment
    guidance from the Markdown documentation. The examples now rely on
    automatically generated IDs while retaining the existing port and rank
    requirements.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime or API behavior changes. The documented configuration
    examples no longer ask users to set `engine_id` manually.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ran Markdownlint on the changed Markdown files.
    - Ran `git diff --check`.
    - Confirmed that the PR does not modify any `.po` files.
    
    Related to #18701.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Signed-off-by: caozq99 <zcao9910@gmail.com>

